WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:15.419
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June eighteenth. The Bank of Japan has raised its interest rate to one percent — something we haven't seen in a very long time. Let's listen.

00:00:16.019 --> 00:00:18.780
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.263
<v News>日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

00:00:25.963 --> 00:00:32.780
<v News>金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

00:00:33.479 --> 00:00:39.408
<v News>金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

00:00:40.107 --> 00:00:45.531
<v News>最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:52.256
<v News>それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

00:00:52.956 --> 00:01:01.283
<v News>金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:07.936
<v News>でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:16.628
<v News>家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

00:01:17.328 --> 00:01:24.096
<v News>これから、私たちの生活がどうなるか、みんなが見ています。

00:01:24.796 --> 00:01:26.427
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:27.028 --> 00:01:33.628
<v Slow>日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:38.268
<v Host>The Bank of Japan raised its interest rate to one percent.

00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:41.004
<v Vocab>金利

00:01:41.403 --> 00:01:49.540
<v Host>It means the interest rate — the cost of borrowing money, given as a percentage. A higher rate means costlier loans.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:57.939
<v Slow>金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:02.748
<v Host>The interest rate is the price of money — what you pay when you borrow.

00:02:03.347 --> 00:02:05.507
<v Vocab>借りる

00:02:05.908 --> 00:02:12.891
<v Host>It means to borrow. Its partner word is to lend: you borrow from the bank, and the bank lends to you.

00:02:13.491 --> 00:02:20.259
<v Slow>金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.804
<v Host>It has been a very long time since the rate was at one percent.

00:02:25.403 --> 00:02:27.948
<v Vocab>久しぶり

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:34.852
<v Host>It means after a long time. You'll also hear it as a greeting — the equivalent of 'long time no see.'

00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:41.668
<v Slow>最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:46.331
<v Host>Lately, the prices of all kinds of things have been going up.

00:02:46.931 --> 00:02:49.020
<v Vocab>値段

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:55.683
<v Host>It means price — how much something costs. You'll see this word on every shelf and menu.

00:02:56.283 --> 00:03:03.147
<v Slow>それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

00:03:03.948 --> 00:03:07.331
<v Host>So the Bank of Japan decided to raise the rate.

00:03:07.931 --> 00:03:10.068
<v Vocab>上げる

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:19.180
<v Host>It means to raise or lift something up. Here the bank raises the rate. The partner verb, to go up on its own, is a different word.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:29.283
<v Slow>金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:35.027
<v Host>When the rate goes up, people who keep savings at the bank earn a little more.

00:03:35.627 --> 00:03:37.812
<v Vocab>貯金

00:03:38.211 --> 00:03:44.620
<v Host>It means savings — money you keep in the bank. The two characters together mean 'store up money.'

00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:52.012
<v Slow>でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

00:03:52.812 --> 00:03:56.075
<v Host>But people who have borrowed money now have more to pay back.

00:03:56.675 --> 00:03:58.979
<v Vocab>返す

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:05.883
<v Host>It means to return something or pay it back — return a borrowed book, or pay back borrowed money.

00:04:06.484 --> 00:04:15.604
<v Slow>家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

00:04:16.403 --> 00:04:20.771
<v Host>Households that borrowed money to buy a home might pay more each month.

00:04:21.372 --> 00:04:23.555
<v Vocab>増える

00:04:23.956 --> 00:04:29.668
<v Host>It means to increase — to grow in number or amount. The opposite is to decrease.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:33.267
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:04:33.867 --> 00:04:36.627
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:04:37.327 --> 00:04:43.112
<v News>日本銀行が、金利を1%に上げました。

00:04:43.812 --> 00:04:50.627
<v News>金利は、お金を借りるときにはらう、お金の値段のことです。

00:04:51.327 --> 00:04:57.255
<v News>金利が1%になるのは、とても久しぶりです。

00:04:57.956 --> 00:05:03.379
<v News>最近、いろいろな物の値段が高くなっています。

00:05:04.079 --> 00:05:10.103
<v News>それで、日本銀行は金利を上げることにしました。

00:05:10.803 --> 00:05:19.132
<v News>金利が上がると、銀行に貯金している人は、もらえるお金が少し増えます。

00:05:19.831 --> 00:05:25.783
<v News>でも、お金を借りている人は、返すお金が増えます。

00:05:26.483 --> 00:05:34.475
<v News>家を買うためにお金を借りた家庭は、毎月のお金が増えるかもしれません。

00:05:35.175 --> 00:05:41.944
<v News>これから、私たちの生活がどうなるか、みんなが見ています。

00:05:42.644 --> 00:05:45.379
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:52.867
<v Slow>日本銀行は、金利を何%に上げましたか。

00:05:53.668 --> 00:05:58.228
<v Host>What percent did the Bank of Japan raise its rate to? One percent.

00:05:58.827 --> 00:06:04.468
<v Slow>なぜ日本銀行は金利を上げましたか。

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:10.067
<v Host>Why did the Bank of Japan raise the rate? Because prices have been going up.

00:06:10.668 --> 00:06:16.836
<v Slow>お金を借りている人は、これからどうなりますか。

00:06:17.636 --> 00:06:21.956
<v Host>What happens for people who have borrowed money? They have more to pay back.

00:06:22.555 --> 00:06:34.939
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.795
<v News>また明日。
